5. Libraries compiled into Pinhole
==============================================================================

5.1 Rust crates (from Cargo.lock; 599 third-party crates in the full
    Windows + Linux dependency tree as of 2026-09-28). Every crate's full
    license text is included in its source package on https://crates.io.

    License summary of the tree:
      MIT OR Apache-2.0 (incl. "Apache-2.0 OR MIT", "MIT/Apache-2.0")  ~360
      MIT                                                               ~140
      Zlib OR Apache-2.0 OR MIT, Unlicense OR MIT, other permissive ORs  ~45
      Unicode-3.0 (ICU4X data crates: icu_*, zerovec, tinystr, yoke…)     18
      MPL-2.0 (cssparser, cssparser-macros, dtoa-short, selectors —
               used by Tauri's build-time HTML processing; option-ext)     5
      Apache-2.0 (tao, gethostname, sync_wrapper, zopfli)                  4
      ISC (rustls-webpki, untrusted, libloading)                           3
      BSD-3-Clause (subtle, alloc-no-stdlib, alloc-stdlib; brotli is
               BSD-3-Clause AND MIT)                                       4
      Apache-2.0 AND ISC (ring)                                            1
      BSL-1.0 (clipboard-win, error-code)                                  2
      Zlib (foldhash, zlib-rs)                                             2
    No GPL/AGPL/LGPL-only crates. (Crates offered under "… OR LGPL-2.1+"
    are used under their MIT/Apache-2.0 option.)

    Direct dependencies:
      tauri, tauri-build, tauri-plugin-dialog, tauri-plugin-opener,
      tauri-plugin-clipboard-manager ......... Apache-2.0 OR MIT
      serde, serde_json, serde_yaml, thiserror, anyhow, async-trait,
      reqwest (rustls), url, sha2, hex, base64, flate2, tar, image, png,
      crc32fast, chrono, uuid, rand, parking_lot, futures-util, dirs,
      fs2, keyring, libc, windows-sys, tempfile .... MIT OR Apache-2.0
      tokio, tokio-util, zip, sysinfo ............ MIT

    To regenerate: `cargo metadata --format-version 1` lists every crate
    with its `license` field.

